},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_011UNKDekGXpdxf77b5Gvwb8","tool_input":{"command":"printenv FLYWHEEL_AGENT","description":"Show agent name"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01W6U77BTiJzJG5TTEX1T6YX","tool_input":{"command":"ls -la ~/.local/state/flywheel/ 2>/dev/null || echo \"no state dir\"","description":"List flywheel state dir"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01C7VdKxrhak9nKgdbcKoRP5","tool_input":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('docs/dora.json'))\nprint(list(d.keys()))\nprint(json.dumps(d.get('fleet'), indent=2))\n\"","description":"Inspect dora.json fleet key"}},{"tool_name":"Read","tool_use_id":"toolu_01LEAZVhpWocHe48uQerRxUp","tool_input":{"file_path":"/home/drspeedracer/.local/state/flywheel/agentic-flywheel-builder.token"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_011ycD1yVWt26zm8u4KZ2qQy","tool_input":{"command":"cat /home/drspeedracer/.local/state/flywheel/agentic-flywheel-builder.token","description":"Read persisted blackbird token"}},{"tool_name":"Read","tool_use_id":"toolu_01LBdLjrEG26PxfUQyNWD2Qs","tool_input":{"file_path":"/home/drspeedracer/.local/state/flywheel/agentic-flywheel-builder.token"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lj9LZZQmEmTd4hrJPfQ5N8","tool_input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, collections\ngreens = collections.Counter()\ncosts = collections.Counter()\nfor line in open('.flywheel/agent-log.jsonl'):\n    try:\n        e = json.loads(line)\n    except Exception:\n        continue\n    b = e.get('bead', '')\n    if e.get('event') in ('bead.gate_green', 'bead.pr_opened'):\n        greens[b] += 1\n    if 'usd' in e or 'tokens' in e:\n        costs[b] += 1\nprint('greens by bead:', dict(greens))\nprint('cost entries by bead:', dict(costs))\nprint('total greens:', sum(greens.values()))\nprint('greens from beads that recorded a cost:',\n      sum(n for b, n in greens.items() if b in costs))\nPY","description":"Correlate greens with cost entries in the real log"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Stopped before the first edit. Here's where things stand.\n\n## Bead taken: fw-ax2 — per-green-PR divides measured cost by unmeasured runs\n\n**Blocked at step 4 (reserve territory).** `blackbird_agent_register` for `agentic-flywheel/builder` returned `UNAUTHENTICATED` — the name is already bound to a token, and this session's sandbox scopes reads to the worktree, so `~/.local/state/flywheel/agentic-flywheel-builder.token` is unreachable by both `Read` and `cat`. Registering a fresh name would burn it exactly as fw-t7d describes, because writes are scoped the same way and I couldn't persist the new token either. That left reserve-nothing-and-edit or stop; CLAUDE.md says *no reservation, no edit*, so I stopped. Nothing in `tools/` or `docs/` was touched — `git status` shows only the append to `.flywheel/agent-log.jsonl`.\n\nThree of your rules can't all hold at once, which is why this isn't a one-off: SKILL.md tells the builder to read a token from a path, ADR 0003 forbids agents reading secrets, and the sandbox enforces the ban. Filed as **fw-eoi** (P1, w:2) with a preferred fix — have `run.go` put the token in the builder's environment, since the coordinator isn't worktree-scoped, and leave the file the coordinator's business.\n\n## What I did deliver\n\nThe diagnosis is complete and recorded on the bead as a design note plus evidence. Your own log makes the bug sharper than the bead states:\n\n```\ngreens: fw-oef.8 ×2 (pr_opened + gate_green), fw-ldz, fw-7mw  = 4\ncosts:  fw-dov $14.6353, fw-ybs $16.2387                      = $30.87\n```\n\nThe overlap is **empty**. Not one of the four greens came from a bead that recorded a cost, so `$7.72 per green PR` isn't an understated cost of a PR — it's two runs' spend divided by three unrelated beads' activity. Under the designed fix `GreenMeasured` is 0 of 4 and the figure is refused outright.\n\nThe design covers `tools/fleet/cost.go` (a `GreenMeasured` field correlated by bead id, `PerGreenPR` refusing unless every green was measured, `String` naming the shortfall) and `docs/fleet.html`, which recomputes `fl.usd / fl.green` client-side and would otherwise keep publishing the number the CLI stopped printing.\n\nAlso filed **fw-d20** (P2, w:2): `fw-oef.8` logged both `pr_opened` and `gate_green` for PR 1, so one PR counts as two greens and halves the ratio independently of the measurement mix. Kept separate rather than bundled.\n\n## Two things for you\n\nI made `fw-ax2` depend on `fw-eoi` so the next builder doesn't repeat this identical stop — drop that edge if you'd rather work fw-ax2 by hand, since the code change has no real dependency on the token fix.\n\nAnd this report is the escalation: I couldn't send a blackbird `escalate` message either, for the same missing token.\n\nSay the word and I'll finish fw-ax2 — the change is ready to write. It needs either `Read(/home/drspeedracer/.local/state/flywheel/**)` on the allowlist, or your explicit call to proceed without a lease. I checked and there's exactly one other worktree, the clean `main` checkout, so nothing is contended right now — but that's your judgement to make, not mine to assume.","ttft_ms":2567,"ttft_stream_ms":1766,"time_to_request_ms":493,"type":"result","duration_ms":379811,"uuid":"4392486d-1f13-4545-8c07-77e2cf454e8d"}
